# Example config for scripts/backup_reflex_db.sh.
#
# Copy this file to:
#   ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/reflex-backup/env
# (or point REFLEX_BACKUP_ENV at wherever you keep it), fill in real values,
# then: chmod 600 <that file>
#
# This becomes a real credentials file once filled in. Never commit it, and
# never leave a filled-in copy anywhere under this repository.

# --- Repository location: pick exactly ONE destination -------------------

# Backblaze B2 example:
# RESTIC_REPOSITORY=b2:my-bucket-name:reflex-db
# B2_ACCOUNT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# B2_ACCOUNT_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# SFTP example (uses your ssh config/keys; no extra vars needed here):
# RESTIC_REPOSITORY=sftp:user@backup-host:/path/to/reflex-db-repo

# --- Repository password --------------------------------------------------

# Preferred: a file holding only the password, chmod 600.
# RESTIC_PASSWORD_FILE=/home/you/.config/reflex-backup/password

# Discouraged fallback, used only if RESTIC_PASSWORD_FILE is unset:
# RESTIC_PASSWORD=change-me

# --- Retention (optional; these are the script's own defaults) ----------
# KEEP_DAILY=14
# KEEP_WEEKLY=8
# KEEP_MONTHLY=12

# --- Source DB path (optional; defaults to this repo's reflex.db) -------
# REFLEX_DB=/home/banar/Desktop/links-bio/reflex.db

# --- Staleness threshold for `restore-test` (optional) -------------------
# Must be a non-negative integer (hours); any other value fails fast with a
# config error instead of silently always passing/failing the check.
# MAX_SNAPSHOT_AGE_HOURS=48
